preConditionHook:
// THE SESSION GAPPED AGAINST THE POSITION AND BROKE THE OPENING RANGE THE WRONG
// WAY -- Grimes: "if the market opens down and immediately presses lower, or
// breaks lower out of an opening range, there is a good chance it could trend
// down all day. Long positions should be dumped immediately."
//
// TWO SESSION FACTS, both fixed early in the day and read all day: the GAP SIGN,
// captured on the session's first bar from this bar's open against the previous
// bar's close (on a session's first bar, the previous session's final close),
// and the OPENING RANGE, the extremes of the session's first openingBars bars,
// frozen once that many have printed.
//
// SESSION MODEL, per the standing decision and identical to OpeningRangeBreakout
// and OpeningRangeMeasuredMoveTarget, the form copied here: a session starts
// when the wall-clock close date changes -- EL's date > date[1], mirrored as
// day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1)) -- and the running extremes plus a
// bars-into-session counter live in locals reset there. barsIn is 1 on the
// session's first bar. Intraday only.
//
// THE GAP IS LATCHED IN BOOLEANS, never in a price local with a sentinel: these
// are back-adjusted futures, 0.0 and -1.0 are legitimate prices and a sign test
// on one is not shift-safe. The quantity tested is the DIFFERENCE
// open[0] - close[1], so the whole rule passes the shift test.
//
// minGapTicks is the minimum gap that counts, in TICKS, written division-first
// as ticks * (ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale()) to match EL's
// ticks * (MinMove / PriceScale), computed once per bar into a local. At its
// default 0 the test is the merged pseudocode exactly -- any gap at all,
// strictly -- and a grid can raise it to ask for a real gap.
//
// WARM-UP mirrors EL exactly: barsIn, orHigh, orLow hold their initial 0 and
// both flags their initial false if the first calculated bar falls mid-session,
// so nothing can fire before the first date change. Mirrored, not corrected.
//
// The corpus's opening-range exits are TARGETS; none reads the session's gap
// direction against an open position. OpeningRangeMeasuredMoveTarget re-read
// against its JSON: no overlap beyond the shared session block.
//
// All state is in localVariables, never at hook scope, so the rule survives
// double placement.
tickSz = ctx.MinMove() / ctx.PriceScale();
if (day_of(ctx.Time(0)) > day_of(ctx.Time(1))) {
    barsIn = 1;
    orHigh = high[0];
    orLow = low[0];
    gapDown = el_gt(close[1] - open[0], minGapTicks * tickSz);
    gapUp = el_gt(open[0] - close[1], minGapTicks * tickSz);
} else {
    barsIn = barsIn + 1;
    if (barsIn <= (int)openingBars) {
        if (el_gt(high[0], orHigh)) orHigh = high[0];
        if (el_lt(low[0], orLow)) orLow = low[0];
    }
}
